      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 140,
      "outputTokens": 1053,
      "costUsd": 0.009547,
      "pronunciationText": "So how do we jump straight to any term? Start at the first term, a, one chair. To reach the second term, add one d. The third term is two d's along, and the fourth term is three d's along. Each time, the number of steps is one less than the position, because the first chair needed no step at all. So the nth term is a, plus n minus one lots of d. Now test the guess. A stack of twenty chairs is nineteen steps above one chair. That's eighty plus nineteen sixes, which is one hundred and ninety-four centimetres, not two hundred. The guess added one chair too many."
    },
