      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 130,
      "outputTokens": 985,
      "costUsd": 0.00893,
      "pronunciationText": "Let's use the formula. An arithmetic sequence has first term five, and common difference three. Find the tenth term. That's nine steps of three after the first term, so a sub ten is five plus twenty-seven, which is thirty-two. Now, which term equals fifty? Set the formula equal to fifty. Five, plus n minus one lots of three, equals fifty. Take away five, and n minus one lots of three is forty-five. Divide by three, and n minus one is fifteen. So n is sixteen, and fifty is the sixteenth term. Check: five plus fifteen threes is fifty."
    },
