      "costUsd": 0.0095595,
      "pronunciationText": "Now a decreasing one. An arithmetic sequence starts at seven, with common difference minus four. Which term is the first negative one? The formula gives a sub n equals seven, plus n minus one lots of minus four, which simplifies to eleven minus four n. Set that below zero. Then four n is bigger than eleven, so n is bigger than two point seven five. But n is a position, so it must be a whole number. The first whole number above two point seven five is three. Check: the terms are seven, three, and then minus one. And the gradient here is minus four, the same as d."
